'' A BODY EDIT REBUILDS ONLY ITS MODULE (RFC-0005 §4): acme.leaf's source changed, so it
'' misses and says which key line did; its interface did not, so acme.middle, which imports
'' it, hits -- and its cached object, linked with leaf's new one, prints the new value. The
'' edit keeps every line where it was: the interface's '#line's say where each declaration
'' is, so an edit that moves one changes the interface too.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_MODCACHE=build/.mct-body/cache
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.mct-body
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/modcache => build/.mct-body
'' STEP: -v -target windows-x86_64 -i build/.mct-body/libs build/.mct-body/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-body/app.exe
'' WRITE: build/.mct-body/libs/acme/leaf/leaf.bas :: '' The bottom of the module-cache fixture: acme.middle imports it, main imports acme.middle.\n#module "leaf"\n#include once "../../../inc/leafcfg.bi"\npublic function Seed( ) as long\n    return LEAF_BASE + 1\nend function\n
'' ARGS: -v -target windows-x86_64 -i build/.mct-body/libs build/.mct-body/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-body/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.leaf: miss (source leaf.bas
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.middle: hit
'' RUN: build/.mct-body/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  16
